Q: JSX Backend Framework: a Joke or a Problem Solver? A: <p>I'm not sure I see a good reason for JSX other than that it smells React-y. Your readme example could be written as nested function calls:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const App = () =&gt;
  Server(
    { port: 3000 },
    Swagger({ title: &quot;My API&quot;, version: &quot;1.0.0&quot; }),
    Logger({ level: &quot;info&quot; }),
    Cors({ origin: &quot;*&quot; }, Routes({ dir: &quot;./routes&quot; })),
  );

render(App());
</code></pre>
